{"name":"Coco Rum","hex":"#9b7757","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"coco","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Coconut palm.","Coconut, the fruit of the coconut palm."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coco"},{"term":"rum","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2/B language code for Romanian."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A spirit distilled from various preparations of sugarcane, particularly fermented cane sugar and molasses.","A serving of rum."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rum"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rum","blocks":[{"text":"Rum is a liquor made by fermenting and then distilling sugarcane molasses or sugarcane juice. The distillate, initially a clear liquid, is often aged in barrels. Rum originated in the Caribbean in the 17th century, where it was likely first created by enslaved people on sugar plantations, but has come to be produced in nearly every major sugar-producing region of the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/A_glass_of_rum.jpg/330px-A_glass_of_rum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rum","wikidata":"Q83376"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Rum_display_in_liquor_store.jpg/500px-Rum_display_in_liquor_store.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Rum_display_in_liquor_store.jpg/1280px-Rum_display_in_liquor_store.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Rum_display_in_liquor_store.jpg/500px-Rum_display_in_liquor_store.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rum display in a liquor store (United States, 2009)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARum_display_in_liqu